--- !u!114 &831313223
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 831313221}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "How does this work:\r\nClicking 'Start Simulation' will advance you to
    a variable input screen to be able to modify the composition of the meteor to
    your desired preferences. After this you will be able to commence the simulation
    and proceed to stage 1\r\n\r\nIn stage 1, the simulation begins and focuses on
    the meteor's path through space. You will be able to see changes in the meteor\u2019s
    velocity, acceleration and its distance remaining until the next stage. In this
    stage you will have access to a \u201CMain\u201D button which will take you back
    to the main menu. Furthermore, in this stage there are 3 points of user interaction:
    a pause button, a play button, and a time scale slider. The pause and play button
    are self-explanatory while you have control of the time slider for the purpose
    of speeding up the simulation. \r\n\r\nOnce done with this stage you will move
    on to stage 2. This is about the meteor travelling in the Earth\u2019s atmosphere
    and two more factors mass and radius (of the meteor) are added as these are now
    subject to change. In addition, there are two more sliders wind speed and wind
    direction that you will have control over. \r\n\r\nIn stage 3, the simulation
    concludes with the meteor's collision with Earth's mantle. If mass or size reaches
    zero before the mantle distance does it means that the meteor has disintegrated,
    and you will be taken back to the main menu. Upon reach the Earth, the program
    calculates impact details, displaying the impact location, crater diameter, overpressure
    ranges and their effects.\r\n\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
